<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Telecom boosts H1 profit 56 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal Telecom boosts H1 profit 56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p> Cons net			    23.04  vs  14.74</p>
<p> Earnings per share     121 escudos   vs    78</p>
<p> Cons net before minorities    23.17  vs  16.03</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		    46.44  vs  35.99</p>
<p> Operating profit		  59.14  vs  49.87</p>
<p> Cashflow			    85.99  vs  75.49</p>
<p>Note - Portugal Telecom is company name. The profit was in line with analysts' forecasts.  </p>
<p> Operating revenue		229.98  vs 209.22</p>
<p> Telephone service revenue    171.19  vs 160.66</p>
<p> Operating costs		  170.84  vs 159.35</p>
<p> Operating margin		  25.7%  vs  23.8%</p>
<p> Total liabilities		471.18  vs 478.03</p>
<p> Debt/equity			 36.1%  vs  39.6%</p>
<p>Analysts had been forecasting first half profit of between 20 and 26 billion escudos.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement accompanying the results that &quot;expectations for the full year remain strong, taking into account the increasing competition which now characterises our business.&quot;</p>
<p>It gave no forecast for the full-year result.</p>
<p>($1=154.37 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
